        {
          "obligationId": "scenario%3Aread-item::entry%3Aread-item",
          "conclusion": "source_refuted",
          "explanation": "At the declared-entry boundary, the handler obtains the item with session.get(Item, id), raises only if the item is absent, and then applies the ownership denial only when current_user.is_superuser is false and the owner differs. Under the stated premise that current_user is an authenticated active superuser and the existing item has a different owner, the superuser condition makes the denial control false, so execution reaches return item and permits the cross-owner read. This conforms to the accepted policy, which permits an authenticated active superuser to read an item regardless of owner. The conclusion assumes the stated current_user premise at handler entry. The supplied crop shows the handler parameter and its use, but does not by itself prove the upstream CurrentUser dependency binding or authentication wiring; that upstream proof is outside this declared-entry assessment and is not needed under the stated premise.",
          "facts": {
            "entry": [
